{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/815991-demon-the-fallen-possession-and-vessel","id":815991,"title":"Demon The Fallen: Possession and Vessel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-25T03:16:59-08:00","id":815991,"title":"Demon The Fallen: Possession and Vessel","content":"I were wondering: a mortal body gain some benefits from being possessed by a demon? Maybe some sort of super strength, super senses or stop aging like vampires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T06:16:31-08:00","id":816046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/815991-demon-the-fallen-possession-and-vessel#post815991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I were wondering: a mortal body gain some benefits from being possessed by a demon? Maybe some sort of super strength, super senses or stop aging like vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possessed mortals still age, but they never &quot;Decay&quot; as other mortals do giving them a strange form of immortality(as in, if a man was possessed at 25 and aged 45 years, he would still look older with white hair, but still be in his have the same physical, mental and social stats as in his prime.)<br /> <br /> The possessing fallen also can heal their host with faith points the way a vampire uses blood points, and they can soak lethal as the possessing demon reinforces their body.<br /> <br /> Those are the only benefits that a possessed mortal body gets though as vampiric strength and speed are due to the disciplines potence and celerity, which demons don't have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T15:08:01-08:00","id":816448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/815991-demon-the-fallen-possession-and-vessel?p=816046#post816046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The possessing fallen also can heal their host with faith points the way a vampire uses blood points, and they can soak lethal as the possessing demon reinforces their body.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was only in Apocalyptic Form, but I only have the core which contradicts itself on this.<br /> <br /> In short, apart from the decay and resilience/healing, demons give their mortal bodies few enhancements. Demons are much better at changing other people's bodies rather than their own (through pacts).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T20:06:33-08:00","id":816614,"title":"","content":"By the DA Devil's Due rules, possessed mortals can always soak lethal (and, unlike in Demon the Fallen, can also heal in combat and heal aggravated with Faith). By Demon the Fallen, they gain the privilege of soaking lethal in Apocalyptic Form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T09:10:27-08:00","id":820366,"title":"","content":"Thank you to all for your explanations<br /> Right now, I'm trying to build up a chronicle, but a potential player, asked me how exactly a demon can escape from the Hell and how he can find a human host. I replied that a demon is pulled out of Hell when there's a mortal soul which for some reason is attuned with the demon. My interpretation is right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T13:03:10-08:00","id":820522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/815991-demon-the-fallen-possession-and-vessel?p=820366#post820366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you to all for your explanations<br /> Right now, I'm trying to build up a chronicle, but a potential player, asked me how exactly a demon can escape from the Hell and how he can find a human host. I replied that a demon is pulled out of Hell when there's a mortal soul which for some reason is attuned with the demon. My interpretation is right?</div> </div> </div> </div>No clue about in Devil's Due, but in Demon: the Fallen, the basic idea is:<br /> <br /> The abyss was cracked by the Sixth Great Maelstrom, which allowed a bunch of low-power demons to escape. they flew around as their demonic selves for awhile, until they realised that they were being pulled back to the abyss, and so they located bodies with a weak attachment to their souls, kicking the soul out and possessing the body.<br /> <br /> Afterwards, the only real way a demon can escape the abyss and find a host is if they are summoned close to one (ideally a 'soulless' body or one of their thralls). I mean you could probably get back to the crack again and escape that way, but the chance of finding a 'soulless' body before you're pulled back again is low.<br /> <br /> I have no idea how a mortal soul would 'attune' with a demon's, partially because a demon in the Abyss is so hate-filled mortal experiences can't really comprehend (with the exception of those Demons who have recently been cast back after their host was destroyed). For the record, there isn't really a 'hell' in Demon: the Fallen, the abyss is best described as sensory deprivation.<br /> <br /> So unless the player's character has been around for a while or you move the date of the SGM much closer to the present (as in, a few years ago at the most) they were probably summoned by somebody and allowed to possess a body.<br /> <br /> Of course, your game, your rules, if you want a hell and demons being pulled out by 'attuning' with a mortal's soul that's fine, but realise that in canon DtF characters aren't 'true' demons as people think of them until the higher levels of Torment, until then there are more Angels of Humanity, just corrupted from the horrible experience they have endured for the last few thousand years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T15:06:03-08:00","id":820584,"title":"","content":"Basically, sometimes a crack opens in the Abyss and a fallen can pass trought it. Then he roam among humans until he's lucky enough to find a suitable host, otherwise he'll be pulled back to the Abyss? And the Abyss is more like a void place where demons &quot;floats&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T15:27:05-08:00","id":820608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/815991-demon-the-fallen-possession-and-vessel?p=820584#post820584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, sometimes a crack opens in the Abyss and a fallen can pass trought it. Then he roam among humans until he's lucky enough to find a suitable host, otherwise he'll be pulled back to the Abyss? And the Abyss is more like a void place where demons &quot;floats&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite. There is a crack in the abyss, which was opened recently (I think near the year 2000? I don't know when the SGM happened). This is the first and only crack of it's time. Weak demons (essentially the rank and file) can slip out and spend a short amount of time looking for a suitable host, before being pulled back to the abyss. The default DtF character is someone who managed to find a host shortly after the crack opened (which is assumed to be no more than a couple of years before the game began). It's assumed they all possessed mortals, because it's easier, but they can possess objects.<br /> <br /> A demon can also possess a host, mortal or object, if it's provided when they are summoned. That's what the earthbound did, although since they never had a mortal host they all have Torment 10.<br /> <br /> (Note PCs can become earthbound if they lose their bodies and the only one available is an object, but they do not go to Torment 10).<br /> <br /> The Abyss is really weird. If you'd prefer to have Demons trapped in hell go with that, but to try and explain the Abyss.<br /> <br /> You smell nothing. You taste nothing. There is no gravity. No forces act upon you. You can hear each other. You can move about, but can never be close enough to properly touch another of the Fallen, compare it as if you were just brushing past them. You are trapped in a void that is empty, except for each other, no forces, no energy.<br /> <br /> But you can see the world. The world and the humans you loved and fought so hard for. But it's falling, humans are becoming worse, they have lost the glories you tried to teach them. However, you cannot contact them. No matter how hard you scream they do not hear you, for you are not on the same plane as them.<br /> <br /> The torment of the Abyss is not torture, it is not inflicted by an outside force (well, except for the creator). It's watching everything you tried to build decay and be lost, and being able to do nothing. For thousands of years.<br /> <br /> The Fallen will do anything to escape that.<br /> <br /> Note that once the Fallen get out, some of them are fascinated by the achievements humans have made. Although the Fallen might know about electricity, they never managed to make something like the internet. Those who are not consumed by Torment might decided to rebuild the paradise they lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T03:08:23-08:00","id":820859,"title":"","content":"So in a nowdays chronicle all PCs must be demons escaped 16 years ago from the Abyss? And the only other choice is to be a demon summoned trought a ritual by some humans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T03:37:12-08:00","id":820862,"title":"","content":"Or go the standard &quot;Golden Rule&quot; path White Wolf has always advocated and make any personal spin and preference you want out of their material. In the world of house ruling the Fallen could by all means have come from Santa's workshop, so why not anything else you might think up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T13:16:02-08:00","id":821160,"title":"","content":"What was that option in Devil's Due that wasn't in regular DtF?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T19:07:07-08:00","id":823942,"title":"","content":"DD they had to be deliberately summoned out. Usually by some stupid Sorcerer or Mage that bit off more than he could chew.<br /> <br /> As to the OP's latest question: Simplest solution would just be to make the SGM happen later. You really don't want 16 year old demons running about. They get *really* powerful *really* fast. And despite the book's suggestion of one they really have no reason to have a Masquerade other than some Earthbound (who RAW are piss weak and only capable of self destruction anyway) being vaguely threatening to them. Quite the opposite, really. They feed on belief and the more they break the masquerade the more people believe in them. Only really need a masquerade if you introduce other splat factions like the Technocratic Union to stomp on them for getting out of line.<br /> <br /> To put it in perspective: They were freed from hell in 2000. They destroyed the world in 2004.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4017,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","user":"angryicecream","date":". 02-04-2016, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T19:22:52-08:00","id":823956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/815991-demon-the-fallen-possession-and-vessel?p=820859#post820859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in a nowdays chronicle all PCs must be demons escaped 16 years ago from the Abyss? And the only other choice is to be a demon summoned trought a ritual by some humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>new demons could be escaping, maybe they just didn't find a body 16 years ago, maybe the crack in the abyss became larger, maybe several things happened that caused the demon to be released","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T21:47:33-08:00","id":823999,"title":"","content":"I've never grasped the arguments concerning Demon's power levels. Am I reading the wrong rulebook? Outside of exploiting Artifacts to get an enormous range of effects (in principal the particular gimmick of a certain House and the Earthbound), Demons seem mechanically a fair bit weaker than vampires. Their ability to resist mind-affecting and illusions doesn't trump the total lack of blood buffing, lack of ability to accelerate aggravated damage healing (short of the House-specific analogue of Obeah 3- and you better hope your Torment doesn't get too high), and inability to soak lethal unless they've already triggered Apocalyptic (rendering them quite susceptible to ambush), and the generally anaemic character of Lores in terms of direct combat functionality (a lot of it just does bashing damage). Things like Thaumaturgy (not to mention Awakened Magic and the like)) easily replicate or trump a lot of the more utility/creative type Lore effects, and Celerity etc. sure make Fallen look silly in battle. Sure a carefully optimized custom built apocalyptic form can lead to impressive innate combat abilities- but you need to deliberately design it to do that and a random Demon isn't necessarily loaded with too much firepower even in High-Torment form. If people can play Ancillae and Elder chronicles without upending reality, then Demons over a decade old shouldn't be too much of an issue to work around if you actually bother to give them extra points (as the GM it's up to you how much strength they've actually managed to gather over the time period/what their starting state would've been).<br /> <br /> Unless you use Devil's Due rules. Then an out of the gate character with enough Willpower (and Torment if you're willing to tread that road) can readily overpower Werewolves in Crinos etc. while having additional supernatural functionality (of course, there is the issue of power points being independent of experience and gated by your antihumanity stat), not to mention improved baseline resilience relative to Fallen (you lose illusion-penetration in return for base soak lethal, in-combat healing, and the innate ability to accelerate aggravated damage healing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T22:37:54-08:00","id":824026,"title":"","content":"Mostly because like half of their lores can easily one shot people or at the very least stun lock them. Especially if they use them in apoc form and use Resonance. Can easily throw around 10+ dice at dif 3. There are a few really awful lores but also several that are hilariously OP. The problem of a game not getting a proper revision...<br /> <br /> Make friends with (or be) a Malefactor and literally every non magical thing you do is at -3 dif and you can hand these off to the ever increasing legions of minions you've been accumulating so *they* are also at dif 3... Learn Forge 1 yourself and you can have your legions of minions producing these magical trinkets themselves!<br /> <br /> Throw in the social lores and there's your easily assembled army that is slavishly loyal to you... Equipped with magical toys... Teach the ones with 3+ Faith to wield it and suddenly every vampire ever is completely fucked because they're getting banged to death with True Faith (As of DtF Faith 3+ mortals are capable of wielding true faith powers)<br /> <br /> So, now you have assembled a small army of humans that are easily the equal of veteran ghouls and aren't half as prone to murdering each other (or you) in fits of jealousy. Oh, and you can make said small army completely immune to mind control BS which annihilates some of the most potent vampire powers... They can also constantly communicate with you.<br /> <br /> Guess technically someone could steal the forge items but that would require them to know they do anything and aren't just normal shit... Which is rather unlikely.<br /> <br /> And this is before ever introducing a malicious power. Or using a benign power maliciously... Only goes downhill from there. Demons basically have all of the powers of vampires (and more) without any of the nasty drawbacks unless they're high torment. Sure, they can't soak lethal but it's really not hard to avoid ambushes when you've got friends that can see the future and have a vested interest in your survival (especially since Demon doesn't have nearly as much time ambiguity as it should. Rather concrete.)<br /> <br /> Why you kind of have to introduce an outside faction like the Technocracy if you want them to have any desire whatsoever to stay quiet and not absolutely thrash any resemblance to the real world. Sure, they might not flag *themselves* with shows of demonic might but it's not exactly hard for them to act through proxies, especially when they can give their apoc forms and lores to thralls.<br /> <br /> Never understood why people focus so heavily on the stupid &quot;Can't soak lethal normally&quot; thing... Neither can Mages and those fuckers are godlings.<br /> <br /> As to the elder and ancilla comment... Those elder and ancilla chars have a vested interest in *maintaining* the masquerade. Demons have a vested interest in seeing it destroyed utterly. Or at the very least cracked substantially. Once humans fully accept that Demons are totally a thing and can be present on Earth Demons can kind of crack open hell and walk around without hosts. At which point they resume their original power. Or, at least something very close to it comparatively speaking. Even if humanity did decide to fight back against the Fallen it's already far too late for them unless they were fully united (Ha. Right.) (unless you throw in Mages which renders the whole discussion rather moot.).<br /> <br /> It's not a matter of the chars having the power to shatter the masquerade. Rather, it's a matter of motivation. Demons have motive to do so, vampires do not. So, comparing them is a bit silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4017,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","user":"angryicecream","date":". 02-05-2016, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T23:42:31-08:00","id":824053,"title":"","content":"Well, the core difference between Demons and Mages (or DA Fae/Hsien) is that the latter's powers are systematically broken due to being arbitrarily versatile and in some cases scalable (Mage rituals, etc.). Demons are still loaded with a bunch of rigid powers some of which happen to be good- they don't intrinsically have the ability to invent novel supernatural solutions for any given problem. I did acknowledge that Forge 1 specifically was broken. I don't seem to recall powers yielding consistent stun-locking or one-shotting (other than using the insta-kill chance Slayer power- combining the High Torment form with Majesty as an Earthbound to theoretically kill every living thing within thousands of miles always seemed like the most entertaining illustration of the power they were supposed to wield). Some of the Lores I do recall as being extraordinarily anaemic (the wind-cutting thing, Lore of Chaos 1, etc.).<br /> <br /> I'm also not clear on how you plan to get multiple Faith 3+ Thralls- I don't recall actually converting Thralls being a trivial process, and those with Faith above 1-2 are supposed to be extremely rare in the mortal population if memory serves. Mass-ghouling seems a fair bit easier. That said, endowing your Thralls with +20 freebies or whatever it was per Faith point always seemed like the most broken trait for raising an army- turn every random joe into a highly trained killer overnight!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","user":"Andkat","date":". 02-05-2016, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T08:41:17-08:00","id":824344,"title":"","content":"Celestials 2 is completely unsoakable, Storms 1 can drown someone in their own spit (admittedly does not work on vampires but it would incap anyone with a working set of lungs as they try to get all the water out...) Portals 3/Realms 2+ randomly dropping off C4 in someone's lap and beaming out, Firmament 4 remotely nuking people, Forge 1 was already discussed, Forge 4 can have hilarious artifacts that make you completely invulnerable, Radiance 4 &quot;Let none raise a hand for violence in my presence&quot;, Radiance 2 &quot;YOU SUCK!&quot;, and that's just off the top of my head for directly dangerous lores.<br /> <br /> Most mortals are faith 1 or 2. Faith 3 basically means you're willing to face discomfort or intense inconvenience for your beliefs. Between Patterns and Celestials it's not at all hard to find such people. Between Longing and Radiance it's not at all hard to inspire people to *become* faith 3+. Mass ghouling only results in a bunch of codependent drug addicts that will kill each other (and you) over the slightest bullshit. Codependent drug addicts whose habits you have to keep feeding and who flip the fuck out if you dare to pay more attention to one than the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T19:07:54-08:00","id":824746,"title":"","content":"To be fair, &quot;I summon your blood into your lungs with this level 1 power&quot; is on about the same level as &quot;I use obtenebration 3 to summon a tentacle in your brain from the shadows of your skull&quot; (in terms of something clearly inconsistent with the intent of the power).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T21:45:27-08:00","id":824817,"title":"","content":"Considering you can actually see the spit I would put it in the same league as summoning an arm of ahriman in someone's mouth. Which is something done in canon a couple of times. Absolutely wrecks mortals. Vampires not so much (unsoakable agg teeth and all that)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T06:35:06-08:00","id":824914,"title":"","content":"First off, one-on-one, demons complete wreck vampires at their supposed specialty (social). You though you could use Presence, Dominate, Auspex 4, or whatever on me? Immunity to mind-changing effects. Don't even try Obfuscate, Chimerstry isn't going to be useful either so don't locate a Ravnos, immunity to illusions.<br /> <br /> Not going into the bag of worms that is thaumaturgy, blood buffing and soaking lethal is a thing, but a demon expecting a fight can just roll Faith and assume Apocalyptic form. They don't care about the Masquerade, if it actually broke down and people started truly believing in demons they might even have a better deal than what they had before the fall (IIRC angels didn't get ability dots, they could instead spend faith to add dice per roll). That brings them up to soaking lethal, gives them a few benefits (like flight for some, as soon as the Demon takes flight several splats start having trouble). Then they fire off whatever deadly evocations they have at levels 1-3 (remember, an evocation at less than 3 dots doesn't cost a faith point, it can be spammed).<br /> <br /> If you're saying that 'vampires have celerity', I believe Demons get a better version as part of Lore of the Fundament (four dots?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T10:49:43-08:00","id":825005,"title":"","content":"Firmament 4 is some strange permutation of Potence moreso than it is an analog to celerity (you generate automatic damage successes which can then be 'split among multiple target')- the main celerity like aspect is that it can increase movement speed. It certainly isn't analogous to making multiple full dice pool attacks per round (Devil's Due does provide the opportunity to purchase a directly analogous power)..<br /> <br /> Demonic immunity is worded specifically around mind control. Auspex 4 should still work (and in Devil's Due, the somewhat analogous Daimoinon Sense the Sin power works just fine against demons). The wording of the ST guide in regards to Vampiric mind control is fixated entirely on Dominate, so it's ambiguous as to whether some of the more subtle Presence effects and the like fall strictly under 'mind control' as Demon considers it. Illusion resistance still requires a roll so Obfuscate and Chimerestry still have a finite chance of working (although the 'social superiority' argument is one generally leveraged in Vampires vs. Garou/Mages, not in respect to Demons who have similar faculties and dependencies). <br /> <br /> Breaking the 'Masquerade' still has consequences in terms of attracting attention from hunters and the wrong kinds of supernatural depending on crossover density. Ease of Reaping/Thrall generation is still counterbalanced by the increased exposure to scrutiny and potential threat occaisoned by any supernatural going for massive exposure.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T11:07:41-08:00","id":825014,"title":"","content":"radiance is basically high powered presence fluff wise and it doesn't work so not sure why presence would work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T13:14:59-08:00","id":825070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andkat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/815991-demon-the-fallen-possession-and-vessel?p=825005#post825005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Breaking the 'Masquerade' still has consequences in terms of attracting attention from hunters and the wrong kinds of supernatural depending on crossover density. Ease of Reaping/Thrall generation is still counterbalanced by the increased exposure to scrutiny and potential threat occaisoned by any supernatural going for massive exposure.</div> </div> </div> </div>But is that alone enough to stop them?<br /> <br /> Demons have an amazing array of social oriented powers and as has been pointed out many of the lores are overpowered. Not to mention the fact that demons don't really Need their host bodies, if they die and are sent to the abyss they can honestly just come back a year later with a fresh identity. So what's stopping a determined demon from going through with it, especially if he has a backup plan for when things go belly up(like a couple of hidden thralls they can possess if their current host is destroyed.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T18:33:43-08:00","id":825181,"title":"","content":"Don't you lose permanent Faith whenever your host dies? That stuff is not exactly cheap and it can erode down to zero (which I think is indeed game over). You can't just keep exposing yourself with every iteration whenever tactically useful without real risk. Not to mention getting soulsucked by an opportunistic peer after getting backed into a corner, or just the ever-present risk of getting dragged back into the Abyss given sufficiently bad luck for who knows how long (quite possibly long enough for the world to end before you get out again, if you are playing Demon in the &quot;leadup to the apocalypse&quot; context it was originally written in).<br /> <br /> But yes, I do concede that Fallen demons can get really terrifying given the right combination of lopsidedly powerful Lores (I somehow did wind up only reading through the Lores that were &quot;cool and thematically interesting but not usually earthshattering on a tactical or practical scale&quot; back when I skimmed through those mechanics...). I mean, the Celestials 4 High Torment Spirit Bomb thing can instantly wipe out or cripple an entire coterie with a good roll... That said, the ability of a Demon to do broken things does hinge specifically on certain particular power/form sets, rather than on something pervasive throughout all members of the splat (a 'vampire' or a 'werewolf' will always have a certain scalability of physical threat regardless of nature- likewise, Magi and Fae have powersets that are universally hyper-flexible and thus will always find a way to do something broken or crazy regardless of the exact combination short of willfully gimping yourself). At the end of the day, like Obtenebration and Celerity in vampire (which do represent a qualitative departure from the typical power level range of vampires in their VtM R/V20 forms), it's feasible enough to mechanically hack and tweak the things that will render older PCs unfeasibly broken if you want to start with experienced characters and are afraid of people beelining the most exploitable abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","user":"Andkat","date":". 02-06-2016, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T22:51:41-08:00","id":825285,"title":"","content":"Originally, yes. But, once they started introducing demon summoning in the ST's guide demons now auto gain the Faith rating of their host at minimum... So, really they can never get below Faith 1. No matter how bad they fuck up. Biggest risk to a Demon is getting killed by other Demons and we're mostly focusing on their ability to fuck up humanity and other supernaturals in these posts. Chances of getting sent back to Hell exist... But, highly unlikely unless you fuck up bad.<br /> <br /> Most Demon powers are hideously broken if you use a bit of imagination. Honestly, the only ones I know of off the top of my head that are just awful are Humanity, Flames, and Light. The rest can very easily be used creatively to wreak utter havoc. Light and Humanity are good to some extent... Just not really within setting since Demons and any high ranking thrall is immune to that shit and they're gonna be the main antagonists. Flames is just shit RAW. Not really any arguing around that. <br /> <br /> Mages can do whatever the fuck they want because Mages, yeah. Not going to argue against the supremacy of Mages in WoD RAW. Changelings can get killed by a mall or just about any government bureaucrat so I tend to not really consider them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T23:30:00-08:00","id":825291,"title":"","content":"I meant Fae/Changelings from Dark Ages (who get Mage-esque flexibility and don't have Banality etc. mechanics, plus an apocalyptic form analogue that can grant lethal soak and some tame form bonuses albeit at the risk of greatly aggravating their splat weakness) rather than CtD Changelings.<br /> <br /> Powers like Fist of Air have also always stuck with me, in the sense of &quot;a gun seems like a much cheaper way to achieve the same effect&quot;. Cyclone effectively amounts to &quot;AoE bashing damage that you need to sustain with Faith&quot; in combat, and is similarly not really very impressive for a level 5 power. There are some other Lores that get pretty underwhelming high level powers- say lore of the Wilds, which effectively turns into &quot;Lore of horticulture&quot;.<br /> <br /> That said, it does astound me that the Lore of Flesh at levels 3 and 5 explicitly accommodates for the sort of permanent attribute increases that people always fretted about with Vicissitude and Biothaumaturgy. They sure make anyone who bothered to spend points on physical attributes look awful silly. That said, the actual power level depends heavily on Lore focus and Form design- Demons really lack the core scalability of Crinos's fixed benefits and innate fast healing, the Kiss (Revelation in the corebook is a piss weak mechanic unless you've dumped everything into Faith for months or years of sessions) and blood buffing and guns-as-bashing-which-is-halved, or flexible powers that always give you something to do- it's not like you get a dozen lore dots at character creation, after all and the apocalyptic form design rules impose some painful constraints, so it's quite possible to end up with demons rather mediocre compared to other supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","user":"Andkat","date":". 02-07-2016, 02:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T23:44:29-08:00","id":825295,"title":"","content":"Wilds is amazing. Can concoct all manner of insane ass plants and poisons. Winds is admittedly another fairly bad one. Missed that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T03:40:17-08:00","id":825345,"title":"","content":"I honestly think arguing about a Demon's ability in combat with other splats is a bit silly, because the majority of Demons are going to be packing several plans in order to avoid combat, from mind-whamming their opponents to locating a path that gets them far away, fast. Demons aren't really meant to interact with other splats, and have a variety of ways to launch an effective one-hit-kill on their opponents (even if they lack 'save or die' powers). Many Demon lores are actually insanely powerful outside of combat, I remember Patterns as possibly being annoyingly useful if you wanted to shortcut information, Paths and Portals renders environmental obstacles (such as walls) moot, and more which I can't remember because I don't have access to my book.<br /> <br /> Using guns on opponents will also run into issues of illegality. Once you start killing the cops because they found out you're killing people it becomes one of those plans, where the dirigible is in flames, everybody's dead, and you've lost your hat. Well, I mean you could just mind-whammy the police and convince them to let you go, but who knows what kind of problems that will create?<br /> <br /> In reference to Reaping, blowing the masquerade won't make it any easier. On the other hand, it will make Faith 3+ thralls more common, allowing demons to build more profitable cults. In all honesty, demons just don't care about any sort of masquerade, and will probably blow it by accident.<br /> <br /> Also, I always considered Humanity a lore where you took a single dot just in case the ST threw languages at you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T05:01:12-08:00","id":825358,"title":"","content":"The thing with Demon and the Masquerade is this : The game is meant to shatter the Masquerade. The world is ending or at the very least it is going to change again. Humanity has reached a crucial moment, many things are in motion (the underworld devastated, mages loosing alot of their assets thanks to the avatar storm, vampire gods awakening) and the Abyss has cracked. The Demons got free again because of the imminent change and they will be a catalyst to steer and faciliate said change. Demons WILL break the Masquerade, first in small amounts and then increasingly more (see Devils Night). It's just the nature of the game. Demons are monsters that want to devour the world and paragons of humanity. The time for hiding has passed, the second war of wrath is imminent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T09:28:01-08:00","id":825442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/815991-demon-the-fallen-possession-and-vessel?p=825358#post825358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with Demon and the Masquerade is this : The game is meant to shatter the Masquerade. The world is ending or at the very least it is going to change again. Humanity has reached a crucial moment, many things are in motion (the underworld devastated, mages loosing alot of their assets thanks to the avatar storm, vampire gods awakening) and the Abyss has cracked. The Demons got free again because of the imminent change and they will be a catalyst to steer and faciliate said change. Demons WILL break the Masquerade, first in small amounts and then increasingly more (see Devils Night). It's just the nature of the game. Demons are monsters that want to devour the world and paragons of humanity. The time for hiding has passed, the second war of wrath is imminent.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the things that many of us keep trying to tell people, the masquerade falling is an inevitability. There are a thousand things that want it gone and it doesn't matter if it's the technocrats, the camarilla, pentex or autumn people, they can't keep it up forever. Humanity Wants to believe in the supernatural and the supernatural wants them to believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T18:27:03-08:00","id":825687,"title":"","content":"the biggest issue demons have with using their powers or apoc form heavily is it opens them up to having their true name figured out.<br /> <br /> if you house rule that out a little then demons have no reason to maintain any kind of hiding from the populace that they know of right off the bat.<br /> <br /> also some of your greatest demon powers come from the effects you can generate from rituals and the bastions you can create","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}